reader-read
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: the operator's ask — read the environment BY THE TYPE READ
  (`read[Env][User]`, `read[Env][Feed]`) rather than one record at a
  time. No new effect and no new handler: `Has[E, T]` is the accessor
  (the induction `HMap.Select` already does over a tuple, keyed by the
  value's type instead of a key val), and `read` is a projection of
  the Reader the library already has. Membership is a compile-time
  fact — a type the environment does not hold does not compile — and
  nothing casts. Derivations: tuple, the whole environment, and any
  product through its Mirror. Also documents the four routes side by
  side (one record, read[E][T], Tag.Of, wire/providing).
files: src/main/scala/Reader.scala, src/test/scala/TestReaderHas.scala,
  docs/typepedia.md, docs/many-instances.md, CHANGELOG.md
